# Laziness proof: $reduce result remains lazy until forced
# The reduce builds an accumulator that would error if fully materialized,
# but we never access the error-producing key, so the error never fires.
# This proves that $reduce returns a lazy dict, not an eagerly materialized one.
[reduce [fn [acc x] [sum: [+ acc.sum x]  error_key: [/ 1 0]]] [sum: 0  error_key: 0] [1 2 3]]
---
%.sum
=== out
Int(6)
=== warn
cannot unify Seq[?] with [0: 1 1: 2 2: 3] at 4:86-4:93
field 'sum' not found in [] at 6:1-6:6
